{"base_rate":0.23622047244094488,"brier":0.12013897637795275,"bss":0.3341163058419244,"bss_hi":0.43788324385816063,"bss_lo":0.2225454088710454,"chart":{"base":[266.2,153.9],"fp":[270.6,190.8],"lead":"62,251.9 272,240.2 482,217 692,188.2","note":{"base":"skill 0.33 — higher than 63% of cities","fp":"low end +3pp, high end +19pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.1 °C — better than 50% of cities","rel":"promised 2% → rained 6%; promised 92% → rained 72%"},"rel":"72.1,441 278.1,352.5 643,153.1"},"country":"MC","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08156167979002626,"ess":339.2053260992489,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Monaco</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Monaco rain forecast is moderately skilful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>80%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>5%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nNICE, 20.0 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.33, ranked 80 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(40&ndash;141) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>5%</b></td><td class='num'>371</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>7%</td><td class='num'><b>9%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>20%</td><td class='num'><b>18%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'><b>35%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>83%</td><td class='num'><b>63%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>85</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Monaco</b> <span class=\"muted\">Monaco</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag ok\">Moderately skilful</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;24% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 24% of days.</p><p>The forecast did better.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>0.33</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>40&ndash;141\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Monaco &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Monaco\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.40264150943396,378.07547169811323 83.76582278481011,335.9240506329114 128.9726829268293,275.4634146341464 235.28702702702702,160.52567567567633 352.71746478873246,48.76056338028167 411.0004705882353,18.0 411.0004705882353,26.56470588235294 352.71746478873246,110.28169014084506 235.28702702702702,239.35135135135135 128.9726829268293,337.609756097561 83.76582278481011,372.7848101265823 59.40264150943396,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"296.01574803149606\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"296.01574803149606\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.40264150943396,363.35849056603774 83.76582278481011,349.746835443038 128.9726829268293,315.4146341463415 235.28702702702702,254.1081081081081 352.71746478873246,151.2957746478873 411.0004705882353,90.80000000000001\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 5% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 371 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.40264150943396\" cy=\"363.35849056603774\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 7%&amp;#10;It rained 9% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"83.76582278481011\" cy=\"349.746835443038\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 20%&amp;#10;It rained 18% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"128.9726829268293\" cy=\"315.4146341463415\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 50%&amp;#10;It rained 35% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"235.28702702702702\" cy=\"254.1081081081081\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 83%&amp;#10;It rained 63% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"352.71746478873246\" cy=\"151.2957746478873\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 85 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"411.0004705882353\" cy=\"90.80000000000001\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(24%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Monaco the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.48) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.08).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'>0.080</td><td class='num'>6.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>29%</td><td class='num'>0.158</td><td class='num'>13.8%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>31%</td><td class='num'>0.413</td><td class='num'>8.0%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>0.484</td><td class='num'>8.4%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":43.7384,"lon":7.4246,"n":762,"n_cities":216,"name":"Monaco","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.003962264150943396,"n":371,"obs":0.05121293800539083,"sig":true},{"hi":0.13,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.07278481012658225,"n":79,"obs":0.08860759493670886,"sig":false},{"hi":0.35,"lo":0.13,"mean":0.2004878048780488,"n":82,"obs":0.18292682926829268,"sig":false},{"hi":0.7,"lo":0.35,"mean":0.5008108108108108,"n":74,"obs":0.35135135135135137,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.7,"mean":0.8325352112676059,"n":71,"obs":0.6338028169014085,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9971764705882353,"n":85,"obs":0.8,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":20.0,"provisional":false,"rank":80,"rank_hi":141.0999999999999,"rank_lo":39.975,"reliability":0.011332262403867012,"resolution":0.0707004964330869,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"monaco","station":"NICE","timezone":"Europe/Monaco"}